65121	65178	63833	63833	Thames	731	“ I do not know . It has long degenerated into a mere personal bickering between the Laureate and Butler . Southey is , of course , revelling in the idea of writing an English work with a Latin title ! and that , perhaps , is the only circumstance for which the controversy is prolonged . ”
65179	65193	63833	63833	Thames	731	“ But Southey , after all , is a man of splendid talents . ”
65194	65211	63833	63833	Thames	731	“ Doubtless ; the most philosophical of bigots , and the most poetical of prose writers . ”
65212	65234	63833	63833	Thames	731	“ Apropos to the Catholic Question , there goes Colonial Bother’em trying to look like Prince Metternich ; a decided failure . ”
65235	65243	63833	63833	Thames	731	“ What can keep him in town ? ”
65244	65260	63833	63833	Thames	731	“ Writing letters , I suppose , Heaven preserve me from receiving any of them ! ”
65261	65280	63833	63833	Thames	731	“ Is it true , then , that his letters are of the awful length that is whispered ? ”
65281	65313	63833	63833	Thames	731	“ True ! Oh ! they are something beyond all conception ! Perfect epistolary Boa Constrictors . I speak with feeling , for I have myself suffered under their voluminous windings . ”
